<Layout title="Methodology">
  <section class="page-heading"><div class="eyebrow">METHODOLOGY</div><h1>Know what<br /><em>you compare.</em></h1><p>The repository separates source evidence, canonical observations, derived measures and presentation.</p></section>
  <div class="prose"><section><h2>Four layers of evidence</h2><ol><li><strong>Sources:</strong> exact dataset references, retrieval dates, usage terms and immutable permitted downloads.</li><li><strong>Canonical observations:</strong> native periods and units, explicit missing values, source references and independent observation and revision statuses.</li><li><strong>Derived measures:</strong> calculations with named inputs and documented conventions.</li><li><strong>Presentation:</strong> independent topic memberships, reusable chart presets, annotation records and presentation colours.</li></ol></section>
  <section><h2>Time and status matter</h2><p>A completed annual observation, a current reading and a full-year forecast answer different questions. The annual chart workspace preserves observation and revision statuses. Reconstructed lines are dotted, forecasts dashed, provisional observations hollow and revised observations square.</p><p>Observed, reconstructed and forecast values are distinguished from final, provisional and revised publication statuses. Missing values remain missing; they never become zeros or interpolated histories.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Preserve statistical identities</h2><p>Registered and ILO unemployment remain separate. Historical monetary instruments and modern policy rates keep their own identities. Historical bond measures do not become ten-year spot rates by changing a label. Federal and general-government debt retain their institutional coverage.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Calculations with clear units</h2><p>Growth is a percentage change in a compatible level series. Rebased indices use a fixed documented base period. Subtracting two yields stored in percent produces a difference in percentage points.</p><p>The first preparation tools support annual growth, rebasing and aligned spreads. Native-frequency aggregation and more advanced analysis will be added after the relevant definitions have been verified.</p></section>
  <section id="publication"><h2>Publication standards</h2><p>A source audit must establish the exact dataset, statistical definition, coverage, revision practice and redistribution evidence. Only verified, permitted real observations enter public downloads.</p><p>Software uses the MIT licence. Each dataset retains its own usage terms, attribution and conditions. The software licence does not grant rights to third-party observations.</p><p>Updates are reviewed before publication. Validation checks provenance, snapshot integrity, periods, duplicate observations and reproducibility. The website is built from committed inputs and makes no live requests to economic data services.</p></section>
  <section><h2>What comes next</h2><p>The interactive atlas is available locally with clearly labelled synthetic examples; production awaits verified Swiss observations. Native-frequency exploration, an optional franc layer and a Relationships view are later milestones. Candidate definitions are a research agenda, not statistical findings.</p></section></div>
</Layout>
